treatment of methicillin resistant staphylococcus
aureus (MRSA) pneumonia. He is a known case of
hypertension and on amilodipine and
hydrochlorothiazide. You decide to start him on
vancomycin. Twenty minutes after intravenous
infusion of vancomycin is started, he develops a
generalized erythematous rash all over his body.
There is no respiratory symptom and the vitals are
within the normal range. Which one of the
following is the most likely cause of this
