Emergency Department of the local hospital you
work at after she was found drowsy. She has end-
Stage ovarian cancer and is on methadone,
codeine, paracetamol, naproxen, and diazepam
for pain control. On her way to the hospital, she
was given naloxone 0.4 mg intravenously because
she has pinpoint pupils. On examination, you
notice that her pupils are still pin-point sized, but
she is less drowsy and able to communicate. The
first thing she says to you is that she is still in
severe pain. Which one of the following would be
the most appropriate next step in management?','{"A":"Give her naproxen.","B":"Give her another dose of naloxone.","C":"Give her diazepam.","D":"Give her more methadone for adequate\npain control.","E":"Give her morphine, intravenously."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex Pharma Onco Immuno 2025.pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-5555fda2cf53","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"bb5c536234f066156bed","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex Pharma Onco Immuno 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex Pharma Onco Immuno 2025.pdf","source_page":85,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"b35c7b482092a0666be8","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":1409,"source_qid":"831"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"bb5c536234f066156bed","source_file":"Amedex Pharma Onco Immuno 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex Pharma Onco Immuno 2025.pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":85,"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Oncology/Immunology","stem":"Catherine, 76 years old, is rushed to the\nEmergency Department of the local hospital you\nwork at after she was found drowsy. She has end-\nStage ovarian cancer and is on methadone,\ncodeine, paracetamol, naproxen, and diazepam\nfor pain control. On her way to the hospital, she\nwas given naloxone 0.4 mg intravenously because\nshe has pinpoint pupils. On examination, you\nnotice that her pupils are still pin-point sized, but\nshe is less drowsy and able to communicate. The\nfirst thing she says to you is that she is still in\nsevere pain. Which one of the following would be\