sudden severe chest pain radiating to his back. On auscultation there is a diastolic murmur best
heard over the left sternal border in the second intercostal space. ECG shows ST elevation in
leads Il, Ill and aVF. A CXR is remarkable for a widened mediastinum. Which one of the following
is the most appropriate management?',NULL,'C','The clinical findings of abrupt chest pain radiating to back and a widened mediastinum on CXR
are consistent with diagnosis aortic dissection. The diastolic murmur signifies involvement of the
proximal aorta resulting in aortic regurgitation and decreased blood flow to the coronary arteries
and a consequent myocardial infarction (MI). Thrombolytics (e.g. alteplase) (option A) are
absolutely contraindicated when aortic dissection is suspected.

Aspirin (option B), clopidogrel and other anticoagulation medications are contraindicated as well
due to increased risk of deterioration of the dissection, which is temporarily stable. The
cornerstone of initial therapy in this situation is morphine for pain control (and its partial effect on
lowering blood pressure) and beta blockers to maintain the systolic blood pressure below 120
mmHg. Trans-esophageal sonography should be emergently performed to confirm the
diagnosis.Angiography using CT angiogram (CTA) (option E) is the preferred method if trans-
esophageal sonography is not available.

(Option C) Referring the patient to a cardiology clinic while he is in the hopsital and in urgent need
for intervention is not an appropriate option.',NULL,'Retain the source-era answer for question-bank study; verify current Australian guidance before clinical use.',NULL,'https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1INFtXPcMSG6sWmzHLKGy6ky71qTiyARj&sz=w1600','2025','v2.9.4',1,'source_page_image','{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Cardiology amedex 2025.pdf","supporting_pages":[8],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-1b42fa210764","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"6f7d2b2d5ed6f4c5c8de","record_type":"visual_mcq","source_file":"Cardiology amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Cardiology amedex 2025.pdf","source_page":8,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.8.2-residual-resolver-page-checkpoint-local-render-2026-09-23","parser_mode":"v282_visual_page_asset","text_method":"source_page_image+best_available_text","visual_asset":"visual_assets/Cardiology_amedex_2025__a83b80e8c658/page_00008.jpg","asset_preview_url":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1INFtXPcMSG6sWmzHLKGy6ky71qTiyARj/preview"}',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET source_id=excluded.source_id,source_question_no=excluded.source_question_no,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,system=excluded.system,topic=excluded.topic,clinical_task=excluded.clinical_task,stem_en=excluded.stem_en,answer_key=excluded.answer_key,source_explanation_en=excluded.source_explanation_en,memory_rule_en=excluded.memory_rule_en,image_ref=excluded.image_ref,source_year=excluded.source_year,import_version=excluded.import_version,active=1,options_mode=excluded.options_mode,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,current_answer=excluded.current_answer,current_answer_status=excluded.current_answer_status,current_evidence_json=excluded.current_evidence_json,currentness_risk=excluded.currentness_risk;
