infarction?',NULL,'C','Absolute contraindications for fibrinolytic use in STEMI include the following:

e Prior intracranial hemorrhage (ICH)

e¢ Known structural cerebral vascular lesion

¢ Known malignant intracranial neoplasm

e Ischemic stroke within 3 months

e Suspected aortic dissection

e Active bleeding or bleeding diathesis (excluding menses)

¢ Significant closed head trauma or facial trauma within 3 months

e Intracranial or intraspinal surgery within 2 months

e Severe uncontrolled hypertension (unresponsive to emergency therapy)
e For streptokinase, prior treatment within the previous 6 months

Relative contraindications for fibrinolytic use in STEMI include the following:

e History of chronic, severe, poorly controlled hypertension

¢ Significant hypertension on presentation (systolic blood pressure >180 mm Hg or diastolic blood pressure
>110 mm Hg

e Traumatic or prolonged (>10 minutes) cardiopulmonary resuscitation (CPR) or major surgery less than 3
weeks previously

e History of prior ischemic stroke not within the last 3 months

e Dementia

¢ Recent (within 2-4 weeks) internal bleeding

¢ Noncompressible vascular punctures

e Pregnancy

e Active peptic ulcer

e Current use of an anticoagulant (e.g., warfarin) that has produced an elevated international normalized ratio
(INR) higher than 1.7 or a prothrombin time (PT) longer than 15 seconds

Of the given options, only heavy menstrul bleeding is not an absolute contraindication to thrombolytic therapy.',NULL,'Retain the source-era answer for question-bank study; verify current Australian guidance before clinical use.',NULL,NULL,'2025','v2.9.4',1,'text','{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Cardiology amedex 2025.pdf","supporting_pages":[16],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-25368dcc009f","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"4e7f0db8cb53d3fbd9fb","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Cardiology amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Cardiology amedex 2025.pdf","source_page":16,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"645510ca5916076b48ca","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":14,"source_qid":"224"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v27_same_page_five_structural","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET source_id=excluded.source_id,source_question_no=excluded.source_question_no,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,system=excluded.system,topic=excluded.topic,clinical_task=excluded.clinical_task,stem_en=excluded.stem_en,answer_key=excluded.answer_key,source_explanation_en=excluded.source_explanation_en,memory_rule_en=excluded.memory_rule_en,image_ref=excluded.image_ref,source_year=excluded.source_year,import_version=excluded.import_version,active=1,options_mode=excluded.options_mode,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,current_answer=excluded.current_answer,current_answer_status=excluded.current_answer_status,current_evidence_json=excluded.current_evidence_json,currentness_risk=excluded.currentness_risk;
