would form the basis for diagnosing an acute ST segment elevation myocardial infarction
(STEMI)?','{"A":"Chest pain with elevated troponin.","B":"Chest pain/discomfort that often radiates, is provoked by exercise and relieved by\nrest.","C":"OC. Chest pain/discomfort suggestive acute myocardial infarction in the presence of\nST segment elevation more than 1mm in two contagious leads, or newly\ndeveloped left bundle branch block.","D":"Chest pain/discomfort, ST depression or T-wave inversion, and elevated troponin.","E":"Unprovoked sustained chest pain with 12-lead ECG that might be normal, with ST\nsegment depression, or T-wave inversion."}','C','According to guidelines of Australian Resuscitation guideline (#14), the diagnosis of an
STEMI is established if there are myocardial ischemia symptoms (non-specific in silent Ml)
and either or both of the following:

¢ ST segment elevation greater than one millimeter in two contagious leads in the
presence of symptoms.
e Development of new left bundle branch block.','{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Cardiology amedex 2025.pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-1a95b8b4b5dd","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"d9c4f01678a884db91f8","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Cardiology amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Cardiology amedex 2025.pdf","source_page":48,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"cbdb8095eee87b0bc8ae","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 CVS (2).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 CVS (2).pdf","source_page":124,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"d4460ab4766695e98dd9","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":80,"source_qid":"286"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"five_block_inferred","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"d9c4f01678a884db91f8","source_file":"Cardiology amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Cardiology amedex 2025.pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":48,"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Cardiology","stem":"According to current Australian Resuscitation Council Guidelines, which one of the following\nwould form the basis for diagnosing an acute ST segment elevation myocardial infarction\n(STEMI)?","options":{"A":"Chest pain with elevated troponin.","B":"Chest pain/discomfort that often radiates, is provoked by exercise and relieved by\nrest.","C":"OC. Chest pain/discomfort suggestive acute myocardial infarction in the presence of\nST segment elevation more than 1mm in two contagious leads, or newly\ndeveloped left bundle branch block.","D":"Chest pain/discomfort, ST depression or T-wave inversion, and elevated troponin.","E":"