nin results.","E":"E. Perform stress test."},"source_answer":"B","source_explanation":"This patient as a typical ischemic chest pain as well as an ECG showing ST segment elevation in leads Il, Ill, and\naVF. With these, an inferior ST segment elevation myocardial infarction (STEMI) is a definite diagnosis prompting\nimmediate treatment and reperfusion therapy.\n\nTherapy should be started regardless of the troponin result (option D) because troponin may take up to 6-8 hours\nto become positive, and its negativity does not change the diagnosis and the management plan in this scenario. In\nother words, even with a negative troponin result, the diagnosis is still STEMI and urgent reperfusion therapy is\nrequired.\n\nAccording to National Heart Foundation of Australia, Australian Clinical Guidelines for the Management of Acute\nCoronary Syndromes For patients with ST elevation myocardial infarction (STEMI) presenting within 12 hours of\nsymptom onset, and in the absence of comorbidities that impact the individual’s overall survival, emergency\nreperfusion therapy with either primary percutaneous coronary intervention (PCI) (formerly called angioplasty) or\nfibrinolytic therapy is recommended.\n\nSince this patient is still in the 12 hours window, angiography to located the coronary stenosis or blockage and stent\nplacement to maintain the vessel patent is the first-line treatment choice. In case PCI cannot be performed with\nacceptable delay, thrombolysis (option C) using agents such as alteplase, tenecteplase or reteplase are the\ntreatment of choice.\n\nWith the definite diagnosis of MI and the need for urgent intervention, sending the patient home on aspirin (option\nA),or performing stress test (option E) are incorrect.","source_answer_status":"source_revealed","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"high","currentness_keywords":["age","fibrinol","guideline","management","pci","therapy","thrombol","treatment"],"likely_visual_question":false,"parser_confidence":"medium","parser_mode":"v27_same_page_five_structural","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"9d7312cc319f1cb049e6e394b9eee14a94273088","duplicate_group_id":"exact-9d7312cc319f","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"73d69bc14a38cf62a7da","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Cardiology amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Cardiology amedex 2025.pdf","source_page":62,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"ec8d9e3573bafb28efd7","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 CVS (1).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 CVS (1).pdf","source_page":193,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"5508e864ea2439703b76","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":114,"source_qid":"1574"}]}',1,'v2.9.4','2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z') ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET source_file=excluded.source_file,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,stem=excluded.stem,options_json=excluded.options_json,source_answer=excluded.source_answer,source_explanation=excluded.source_explanation,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,visual_asset=excluded.visual_asset,visual_url=excluded.visual_url,options_mode=excluded.options_mode,current_answer=excluded.current_answer,current_answer_status=excluded.current_answer_status,current_evidence_json=excluded.current_evidence_json,currentness_risk=excluded.currentness_risk,record_json=excluded.record_json,active_quiz=excluded.active_quiz,import_version=excluded.import_version,imported_at=excluded.imported_at;
