aneurysm (AAA)?','{"A":"OA. AAA more than 5.0 cm in a male patient.","B":"B. AAA more than 5.0 cm in a female patient.","C":"C. AAA growth more than 1.0 cm/year.","D":"D. AAA with back pain.","E":"E. AAA with distal thromboembolism."}','A','The following are indications for surgical repair of an aortic aneurysm:

e Asymptomatic abdominal aortic aneurysm greater than over 5.5 cm in men

e Asymptomatic abdominal aortic aneurysm over 5.0cm in women

e Thoracic aortic aneurysm over 6.0 cm

e¢ Growth of more than 1.0c m/year

¢ Symptomatic abdominal aortic aneurysm (abdominal/back pain, distal
thromboembolism)

An asymptomatic aortic aneurysm of 5.0 cm in a male is not an indication for surgical
repair.','{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Cardiology amedex 2025.pdf","supporting_pages":[63],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-f3ab3023f414","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"209a89524a630afce66d","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Cardiology amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Cardiology amedex 2025.pdf","source_page":63,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"f0856e4bf3ade781c032","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 CVS (1).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 CVS (1).pdf","source_page":73,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"5d007397ba5d890173cd","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":47,"source_qid":"258"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v27_same_page_five_structural","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','low','{"record_id":"209a89524a630afce66d","source_file":"Cardiology amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Cardiology amedex 2025.pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":63,"supporting_pages":[63],"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Cardiology","stem":"Which one of the following is not an indication for surgical repair of an abdominal aortic\naneurysm (AAA)?","options":{"A":"OA. AAA more than 5.0 cm in a male patient.","B":"B. AAA more than 5.0 cm in a female patient.","C":"C. AAA growth more than 1.0 cm/year.","D":"D. AAA with back pain.","E":"E. AAA with distal thromboembolism."},"source_answer":"A","source_explanation":"The following are indications for surgical repair of an aortic aneurysm:\n\ne Asymptomatic abdominal aortic aneurysm greater than over 5.5 cm in men\n\ne Asymptomatic abdominal aortic aneurysm over 5.0cm in women\n\ne Thoracic aortic aneurysm over 6.0 cm\n\ne