pedis pulse is not perceptible. The limb feels cold and looks pale. The patient is given analgesics. After starting the patient on
heparin, which one of the following would be the most appropriate step in management?',NULL,'B','This patient has developed critical acute limb ischemia requiring urgent vascular surgery for revascularization and restoration
of blood supply.

Clinical signs of acute arterial occlusion include (6 P''s):

¢ Pain

¢ Paralysis

e Pulselessness
¢ Pallor

e¢ Paresthesia

¢ Poikilothermia.

With any of the above signs or symptoms, the patient is considered to have acute limb ischemia.

To confirm the diagnosis of acute arterial occlusion and the extent of obstruction, the patient should have an urgent CT
angiogram as the road map to the surgery. Magnetic resonance angiography with contrast is an alternative to CT angiography
with about the same sensitivity and specificity.

(Option A) An abdominal CT scan is not required as this patient did not present primarily with abdominal problems.

(Options C and D) Pelvic ultrasound or Doppler Duplex ultrasound of the calf veins adds nothing to the management strategy
because firstly the diagnosis is already made, and secondly these modalities do not provide adequate information regarding
the anatomical site of the occlusion. Furthermore, Doppler Duplex ultrasound is highly operator-dependent.

(Option E) Echocardiography is the investigation to consider once the acute phase of arterial occlusion has been managed.
Thrombi from the heart is a main source of acute limb ischemia.',NULL,'Retain the source-era answer for question-bank study; verify current Australian guidance before clinical use.',NULL,NULL,'2025','v2.9.4',1,'text','{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Cardiology amedex 2025.pdf","supporting_pages":[74],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-ba02477f83f5","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"7591a97f86aee459eb2c","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Cardiology amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Cardiology amedex 2025.pdf","source_page":74,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"5cd8c4295442b43d285d","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 CVS (2).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 CVS (2).pdf","source_page":120,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v27_same_page_five_structural","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET source_id=excluded.source_id,source_question_no=excluded.source_question_no,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,system=excluded.system,topic=excluded.topic,clinical_task=excluded.clinical_task,stem_en=excluded.stem_en,answer_key=excluded.answer_key,source_explanation_en=excluded.source_explanation_en,memory_rule_en=excluded.memory_rule_en,image_ref=excluded.image_ref,source_year=excluded.source_year,import_version=excluded.import_version,active=1,options_mode=excluded.options_mode,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,current_answer=excluded.current_answer,current_answer_status=excluded.current_answer_status,current_evidence_json=excluded.current_evidence_json,currentness_risk=excluded.currentness_risk;
